.TH CF-KV 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-kv.1 \- Manage Workers KV key-value storage namespaces and keys
.PP
Manage Cloudflare Workers KV namespaces and globally distributed key-value data with low-latency reads.
.PP
.PP
.SH REQUIRED PERMISSIONS
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
Read
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers KV Storage:Read\fR
.TP
Write
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers KV Storage:Edit\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS OVERVIEW
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv namespaces\fR (#cf-kv-namespaces) — Manage KV namespaces (CRUD)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv list\fR (#cf-kv-list) — List keys within a namespace
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv get\fR (#cf-kv-get) — Read the value of a key
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv put\fR (#cf-kv-put) — Store a key-value pair
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv delete\fR (#cf-kv-delete) — Remove a key
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv bulk-write\fR (#cf-kv-bulk-write) — Upload up to 10,000 key-value pairs at once
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf kv bulk-delete\fR (#cf-kv-bulk-delete) — Delete keys in bulk
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv namespaces\fR"
.PP
Manage isolated key-value namespaces.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List all namespaces
cf kv namespaces list

# Create a new namespace
cf kv namespaces create --title "SESSION_STORE"

# Rename a namespace
cf kv namespaces rename --id <namespace-id> --title "NEW_TITLE"

# Delete a namespace and all its stored keys
cf kv namespaces delete --id <namespace-id> [--yes]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv list\fR"
.PP
Lists keys within a specified KV namespace.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv list --namespace-id <id> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--namespace-id <id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR KV Namespace ID
.TP
\fB--prefix <prefix>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Filter keys starting with a prefix string
.TP
\fB--limit <number>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDescription:\fR Maximum number of keys to return (default: \fB1000\fR)
.TP
\fB--cursor <cursor>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Cursor token for iterating through large namespaces
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List keys matching a prefix
cf kv list --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --prefix "user:"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv get\fR"
.PP
Retrieves and prints the raw stored value of a key.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv get --namespace-id <id> --key <key-name>
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv get --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --key "user:123:profile"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv put\fR"
.PP
Writes a key-value pair to the namespace, accepting either raw strings or file contents.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv put --namespace-id <id> --key <key> (--value <val> | --file <path>) [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--namespace-id <id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Target Namespace ID
.TP
\fB--key <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Key name
.TP
\fB--value <string>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Direct string value to store
.TP
\fB--file <path>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Read file contents as the value
.TP
\fB--ttl <seconds>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDescription:\fR Relative expiration time in seconds (minimum: \fB60\fR)
.TP
\fB--metadata <json>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR JSON metadata object to store alongside the key
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Store inline string with a 1-hour expiration
cf kv put --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --key "cache:token" --value "secret123" --ttl 3600

# Store contents of a JSON file
cf kv put --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --key "config:site" --file site-config.json
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv delete\fR"
.PP
Removes a single key from a namespace.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv delete --namespace-id <id> --key <key> [--yes]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf kv delete --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --key "user:123:profile" --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf kv bulk-write\fR & \fBcf kv bulk-delete\fR"
.PP
Execute high-volume batch operations against KV.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Bulk write up to 10,000 keys from a JSON payload
# Payload format: [{"key": "k1", "value": "v1"}, {"key": "k2", "value": "v2", "expiration_ttl": 300}]
cf kv bulk-write --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --file batch.json

# Bulk delete keys from a JSON array of strings
# Payload format: ["k1", "k2", "k3"]
cf kv bulk-delete --namespace-id 0f2b3e8c9a --file keys-to-delete.json --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
